WEBVTT

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:30.640
Welcome back.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.480
Well, here we are on the last show

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:34.560
of the ninth television series.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.680
And I'm certainly glad you joined me today.

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:39.180
So for this show, I thought we'd do something

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.910
a little bit different, a nice, happy little painting.

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:43.630
And I've already started out here,

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:47.230
and I've taken liquid black, as you can see,

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:49.690
and went right around here, and then right in the center,

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:51.830
just liquid white, and sort of let them blend together

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:53.360
right here, where they come together.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:55.360
Liquid black is exceptionally good

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:58.580
for areas where you're gonna have a lot of dark shadows,

00:00:58.720 --> 00:00:59.960
very dark colors, you can put that

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.140
saves you a lot of work.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:03.760
So let's have them graphically run all the colors

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:05.520
across the screen that you need

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:07.180
to paint this painting along with me,

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:08.830
and we'll come on up here and get started.

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:13.920
Alrighty, let's start off today with a touch of phthalo blue,

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.960
and we'll just tap a little of that into the brush,

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:18.910
and we can add a little black to that too,

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:19.830
just to dull it down.

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:23.320
There we go, small amount of color.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:24.720
Let's go right up here.

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:26.380
Start right at the top,

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:29.840
and as usual, make our little criss-cross stroke.

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:34.220
Just like so, just like so.

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:36.560
Very nice, easy to do.

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:41.620
And we'll bring it down to about like that.

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:47.300
Okay, and very gently go across

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.480
to take out the brush strokes.

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:51.510
And that quick, we got a happy little sky.

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:55.720
We'll wash our brush, shake off the excess,

00:01:58.620 --> 00:01:59.980
and we'll get the cap.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.800
The cameraman again, he has caught the devil.

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:06.100
I'm gonna go right into titanium white

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.020
and just pull that brush through it.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:09.820
Just tap a little color right into it.

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:11.770
Okay, let's go right up here.

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:13.510
Maybe there's a happy little cloud

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:14.730
that lives up here in the sky.

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:16.830
It just sort of floats around.

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:18.900
See, just sort of pull it around.

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:23.100
Bam, this is just straight titanium white.

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:24.680
And we just want the indication

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:26.160
of a little something happening in there.

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:29.880
We're not looking for a lot of detail far away.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:32.280
There we are.

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:38.510
Okay, and that quick, we have a happy little cloud.

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:41.700
In this series, we've made a lot of different clouds.

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:44.360
We've made some great big stormy clouds

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:47.000
and some with a lot of color in them.

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:51.640
And we've made some beautiful seascapes.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:54.760
I really, really hope you've enjoyed those also.

00:02:55.570 --> 00:02:57.310
Let's build us a little mountain back here.

00:02:57.470 --> 00:02:58.430
Let's take some black.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:03.180
Some Van Dyke brown, a little touch of blue.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:05.680
Shoot, let's throw some crimson in there too.

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:09.400
So we got blue, brown, alizarin, crimson, and black.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:11.750
Pull it out, very flat.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:15.640
Now, cut across and get our little roll of paint.

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:17.760
We always use that little roll of paint, okay?

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:21.630
Now then, we're gonna have a nice little mountain

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:22.870
that lives way back here.

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:25.270
Push that paint right into the fabric.

00:03:26.710 --> 00:03:29.870
Just really push hard, work it in there.

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:34.920
Just push it, there we go.

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:38.060
There he is.

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:39.810
The only thing you're worried about

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:41.330
is this nice outside edge.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:49.460
Okay, we'll take a large brush, grab it and pull.

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:51.640
Let it blend with the liquid white,

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.710
and it just disappears.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.600
right into nothing, just a nice, misty effect.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:08.840
Okay, let's take a little titanium white,

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:12.800
cut us off a small little roll of paint, just a tiny bit.

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:18.530
And let's go up here and just let the knife float.

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:24.880
Just let it float, put in some nice highlights.

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:27.990
And you could do this in colors.

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:29.870
You might wanna, you might wanna.

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:31.770
a mountain that's brown with all kinds

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:37.320
of beautiful rocks and stones works the same way, same way.

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:40.490
So in your world, you decide,

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:43.340
and you make it any way that you want it.

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:47.460
Let's take some white, some phthalo blue,

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:51.590
add a little bit of van dyke brown to that.

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:52.610
There we go.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:55.850
The brown is just used to dull that blue down a little bit

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:57.110
so it's not quite so bright.

00:04:58.180 --> 00:04:59.400
Cut off that little roll of paint.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:03.490
Okay, now then, come right back in here.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:07.110
See there, that easy, it's easy.

00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:09.560
Just put in some nice little shadows.

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:15.280
Just sort of let those work right together, together.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:19.440
And you can wander back in here

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:21.140
and pick up some of the whites.

00:05:22.010 --> 00:05:23.750
Or you can just make all kinds of things

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:27.000
happen in your mouth, all kinds.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:29.040
You're limited only by your imagination.

00:05:31.340 --> 00:05:33.760
Only by that, nothing else.

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:38.810
What you can see in your mind, you can put on canvas.

00:05:44.390 --> 00:05:46.950
An artist, maybe imagination is one of the most important

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:48.980
things that you can possess.

00:05:50.440 --> 00:05:52.140
So, develop your imagination.

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:55.520
It's like any other muscle in the body.

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:59.120
Use it, use it, exercise it, practice with it.

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:02.230
You'll be amazed at what you can imagine.

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:08.760
Pretty soon, if you paint, you become very aware of nature.

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:13.390
You become aware of color, and you're riding down the street

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:15.210
and you'll see a beautiful tree, and you'll say,

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:17.270
oh, look at the sap green in that tree,

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:20.570
or the white in that cloud, that's made with a fan brush.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:23.150
You have to be careful, though.

00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:27.000
You'll get so interested in all the beautiful things

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.460
that nature has, you'll drive right off the road.

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:33.150
I always carry a camera with me,

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:35.180
and I take pictures all over the country

00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:37.380
of the different areas.

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:40.860
Okay, I'll go right back into that mountain color,

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:45.390
and to that I'll add a little more blue,

00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:51.360
a little white, there, I'm looking for a bluish color,

00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:54.220
but not like that, that's a nice color.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:55.980
Okay, let's go right back up here.

00:06:56.780 --> 00:06:59.490
Maybe there's a happy little foothill that lives.

00:07:00.410 --> 00:07:02.120
Right there, see it, see it?

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:03.880
There it is, it lives right there in that brush.

00:07:04.950 --> 00:07:09.300
Just tap it out, tap it out, there.

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:13.260
You know, I think I've mentioned in some of the other shows,

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:18.410
most of the ideas that we use to do paintings

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:20.600
come from people all over the country.

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:24.540
If you have something you'd like to have painted,

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:28.370
drop me a line, I'd love to hear from you.

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:33.580
and some people send postcards or photographs.

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:35.380
Tell me what interests you.

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:38.220
If it's something I can't do, shoot,

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:39.620
we'll go out and get us a guest artist

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:41.340
and we'll bring him in and we'll get them

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:45.010
to show you how to do it, Miguel.

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:47.660
And with the completion of this series,

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:51.630
there are, gosh, 117 shows now.

00:07:52.390 --> 00:07:53.950
If you haven't seen them all in your area,

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:55.300
give your station a call.

00:07:57.320 --> 00:07:58.520
Let them know that you want to see them.

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:03.800
There you go, there you go.

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:06.070
Okay, let's have some fun.

00:08:06.940 --> 00:08:09.710
I'm gonna take, we'll take black,

00:08:10.270 --> 00:08:13.040
we'll put some brown in there, and sap green.

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:16.440
Looking for a very, very dark color.

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:19.920
You can throw some blue in there too, it doesn't matter.

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:24.070
Okay, let me clean my knife off.

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:27.990
Let's grab us a fan brush.

00:08:28.790 --> 00:08:29.830
Load that fan brush.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.920
Full of color, lot of paint in the brush, lot of paint.

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:37.130
Okay, good, let's go up here.

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:40.780
Now then, I wanna do some happy little evergreens.

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:41.980
I like evergreens.

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:47.340
Just use a corner of the brush and go back and forth.

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:53.170
There, give him a friend.

00:08:55.230 --> 00:08:57.720
These get lonely too, we all need a friend.

00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:02.590
There we go, and then maybe, tell you what,

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:04.320
there's another one.

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:05.800
Let's just put a bunch of them in here,

00:09:05.860 --> 00:09:06.640
I like to do these.

00:09:07.870 --> 00:09:09.640
And some, some parts of the country,

00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:11.200
evergreens are real skinny,

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:14.270
and other parts, they're sort of fat,

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:18.310
so either way you want them.

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:20.900
They're made basically the same way.

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:26.660
Trees are like people, they have personalities,

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:29.420
each one's different, each one's an individual,

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:29.860
it's unique.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:33.770
Unique and different, it's really different.

00:09:34.350 --> 00:09:36.220
So, don't worry about it.

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:39.930
If your tree didn't look just like the one you see here,

00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:41.640
that means they're probably better.

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:46.200
We really are not trying to teach you to copy with these.

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:49.320
We're trying to show you how to make effects

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:50.860
and turn you loose on the world,

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:54.260
because you can own the world.

00:09:57.620 --> 00:09:58.540
There, let's see.

00:09:58.700 --> 00:09:59.960
I'll tell you what, I'm just...

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:01.690
going tree crazy.

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:05.630
The more of these little trees you do,

00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:08.990
the more practice you'll get and the easier they'll become.

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:13.810
A good way to practice is just take old canvases

00:10:13.810 --> 00:10:16.790
or something and just do a whole canvas full of trees

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:19.430
or mountains or skies or whatever it is

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:20.810
that you're having problems with.

00:10:21.990 --> 00:10:23.790
The best way to overcome a problem area

00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:25.920
is to do it over and over until you learn.

00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:32.320
There's another happy little tree.

00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:35.800
Another happy little tree.

00:10:40.130 --> 00:10:42.370
Okay, well, we got a mess of trees going in there.

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:44.920
Almost have us a little forest.

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:49.280
So, I'm gonna take some of the dark sienna,

00:10:50.070 --> 00:10:52.240
a little white, cut through,

00:10:52.440 --> 00:10:54.660
have a tiniest little roll of paint

00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:55.720
right on the edge of the knife.

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:56.380
Let's go up here.

00:10:57.200 --> 00:10:59.420
Now, with that, I'm gonna sneak back in here.

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:01.970
And just here and there put the indication

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:03.730
of a little trunk.

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:06.280
We don't want these trees to fall over.

00:11:06.380 --> 00:11:09.500
These are strong trees, happy trees back here.

00:11:11.570 --> 00:11:12.930
Everything we paint is happy.

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:16.580
Your paintings reflect your mood.

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:20.680
You're in a bad mood, you'll paint an angry old painting.

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:23.490
That's when you do the big storm clouds.

00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:26.840
And when you're happy, your paintings will reflect that.

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:29.980
They'll be bright and cheery in the...

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.120
colors will be super.

00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:36.100
All right, tell you what, let's do,

00:11:36.180 --> 00:11:37.560
let's go right into this dark color.

00:11:37.660 --> 00:11:39.220
This was the old tree color,

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:41.380
and I'm just gonna tap this brush right in there.

00:11:42.140 --> 00:11:44.620
Now we need something for all these evergreens to set on.

00:11:45.880 --> 00:11:47.320
Right now, they're just sort of floating around,

00:11:48.180 --> 00:11:51.780
so let's begin, let's begin creating a lay of the land.

00:11:55.170 --> 00:11:57.470
See, if this was a white background here,

00:11:57.570 --> 00:11:59.690
if you had liquid white, this color would be,

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:02.840
Oh, it'd be a lot more difficult to apply

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:05.740
because the dark's already in there.

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:07.650
It just drops in real easy.

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:10.270
I don't know if you can even see it, but it's there.

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:12.190
Now, watch what happens.

00:12:12.270 --> 00:12:17.200
Let me grab another brush, right into some yellow.

00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:22.030
Yellow, I'm gonna reach up here and get some sap green.

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:24.360
So we have yellow and sap green.

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:27.050
And tap this brush firmly into the color.

00:12:28.190 --> 00:12:29.420
Alright, now then.

00:12:30.570 --> 00:12:33.400
Now then, this will really show up against the dark.

00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:37.480
And this is where we want to create, once again,

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:39.060
lay of the land.

00:12:42.580 --> 00:12:44.640
Again, making big decisions here.

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:45.560
How does this go?

00:12:46.670 --> 00:12:50.620
I see little hills, so I'll paint little hills.

00:12:52.560 --> 00:12:55.490
And whatever you see in your painting, in your world,

00:12:55.900 --> 00:12:56.920
that's what you want to paint.

00:12:57.720 --> 00:12:59.060
Look at that, see?

00:12:59.430 --> 00:12:59.970
Just a hill.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:04.500
hill after hill, as many as you want, or as few as you want.

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:09.240
Go right over here, I want this side to be left out,

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:16.020
and if you want it darker, all you have to do

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:18.860
is continually tap, if you just tap on it,

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:20.740
then it's gonna pick up the liquid black,

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:23.280
automatically, it's gonna get darker,

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:26.080
you don't have to worry about it, it just happens.

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:29.890
Okay, I want a stone.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:32.870
Maybe we'll do a bunch of rocks in this one.

00:13:34.090 --> 00:13:38.690
There's a stone that lives right about there.

00:13:39.090 --> 00:13:42.480
There's a nice stone, see?

00:13:44.110 --> 00:13:46.850
How do you make a round stone with a square knife?

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:49.200
That's your project for today.

00:13:50.190 --> 00:13:52.290
They just go right around, see?

00:13:52.410 --> 00:13:54.290
Put some highlight on him.

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:55.510
Look how that stands out.

00:13:56.300 --> 00:13:58.620
That's just some dark sienna with a little white in it.

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:02.600
And that easy, we have a nice little stone.

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:05.530
Now you can take and pull a tiny bit of that color down

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:06.900
and make it look rougher.

00:14:08.270 --> 00:14:11.230
That's what my dog says, rough there.

00:14:13.720 --> 00:14:17.590
Okay, and we'll take a little more of our green

00:14:17.590 --> 00:14:20.260
and yellow mixture right on the brush.

00:14:22.520 --> 00:14:25.700
And let's take, and we come right down here

00:14:25.700 --> 00:14:27.670
at the foot of this rock, see there?

00:14:28.600 --> 00:14:29.980
And that lays him right in.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:33.470
in the painting, isn't that super?

00:14:35.940 --> 00:14:41.940
Layer after layer, okay, maybe, maybe,

00:14:42.170 --> 00:14:44.820
maybe there's another stone, that's right here.

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:46.680
Let's put a bunch of stones in this one.

00:14:47.890 --> 00:14:49.860
They're a lot of fun, a lot of fun.

00:14:49.980 --> 00:14:53.020
There's another one, wherever you want them.

00:14:54.640 --> 00:14:56.200
Tell you what, maybe this is a big stone.

00:14:56.430 --> 00:14:57.590
Let's have a big ol' stone.

00:14:58.660 --> 00:14:58.880
Come on.

00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:01.600
We just get carried away here.

00:15:03.100 --> 00:15:04.680
These stones will, if you're not careful,

00:15:04.780 --> 00:15:06.540
they'll grow and they'll eat up your whole world.

00:15:08.190 --> 00:15:09.670
What started out as a little stone

00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:11.160
turned into a big one.

00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:14.120
And we'll use those same colors,

00:15:14.320 --> 00:15:17.460
just, this is a little bit of dark sienna,

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:20.640
touch of white, and you just let this graze it.

00:15:20.850 --> 00:15:25.840
Just barely touch, it's a delicate,

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:27.620
delicate touch imaginable.

